The object of hhuunntt is to kill off the other players.  There are no rooms, no
treasures and no monsters: you wander around a maze, find grenades, trip
mines, and shoot down walls and players.  The more players you kill before
you die, the better your score.

hhuunntt looks for a game in progress on the local network by broadcasting a UDP
request; if none answers, it starts a driver, //uussrr//ggaammeess//lliibb//hhuunnttdd, on the
local machine.  Naming a _h_o_s_t asks that machine's driver instead, so a game
must already be running there (see hhuunnttdd).  If more than one game answers,
hhuunntt lets you pick one.

