_P_l_a_y_i_n_g

The right of the screen is the status area: damage sustained, charges left,
who is playing, who is scanning (\\*) or cloaked (++), and the scores. The
rest is your map of the maze; line 24 carries messages too long for the
status area.

The movement keys are vvii's: hh, jj, kk and ll move left, down, up and right. 
The upper-case key HH, JJ, KK or LL turns to face that way without moving; you
can only fire or throw in the direction you face. Moving into another player
stabs him.  The other commands are:

ff or 11   Fire a bullet (1 charge)
gg or 22   Throw a grenade (9 charges)
FF or 33   Throw a satchel charge (25 charges)
GG or 44   Throw a bomb (49 charges)
55 .. 99   Throw larger bombs (81, 121, 169, 225 and 289 charges)
00, @@     Throw the two largest bombs (361 and 441 charges)
oo, OO     Throw small or big slime (5 or 10 charges)
pp, PP     Throw bigger or biggest slime (15 or 20 charges)
ss         Scan: show where the other players are (1 charge)
cc         Cloak: hide from scanners (1 charge)
^^LL        Redraw the screen
qq         Quit

The map uses these symbols:

-- || ++     walls              // \\      deflecting walls
##         doors (disperse shots)   ;;  gg    small and large mines
::         bullet             oo OO @@    grenade, satchel, bomb
ss $$       small and big slime      \\*        explosion
>> << ^^ vv   you, facing right, left, up or down
}} {{ ii !!   another player, facing right, left, up or down
??         a wandering bomb, released every 30 deaths or so

Shots move five times as fast as you do, and the gun must cool after three
in a row.  A stab does 2 points of damage, a shot 5, and slime 5 each time
it touches.  You start with 15 charges and get 5 more each time a player
enters. Every explosion is centred on the square it hits and does most
damage there; a grenade covers 3 by 3, the bombs 5 by 5 up to 21 by 21. 
Slime flows around walls over as many squares as the charges spent.  A shot
destroys an ordinary wall; deflecting walls and doors survive shots but not
an adjacent grenade. Destroyed walls regenerate in the order they fell, one
in a hundred as a deflector or a door, and a wall regenerated under a player
throws him some distance and hurts him on landing.  A mine trips with
probability 2% when walked onto forward, 50% sideways and 95% backing up,
costing 5 or 10 points; defusing one is worth 1 or 9 charges.  Cloaking
costs one charge per 20 of your moves, scanning one per 20 times the number
of players of theirs, and turning one on turns the other off.  A kill adds 2
to your damage capacity and takes 2 damage points away.  Typeahead is at
most 5 characters, and if nobody moves, nothing moves.

When you die you are asked whether to re-enter.  Besides yy and nn you may
answer ww, to write a message first, or oo, to change how you enter.

Your score is the decayed average of kills per entry, kept only for the
session.  A running game raises the load average by about the number of
players plus one half.

